00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.740
- Thank you, I'm honored to be with you.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.820
And really honored that
the, whatever tropical storm

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.170
hurricane we were going through,

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.878
seems like it is passing through quickly.

00:02:12.878 --> 00:02:15.870
So people will be safe.
- Okay (laughing) that's,

00:02:17.147 --> 00:02:20.060
that's the honor, well I
guess it's better to go fast

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.320
than to go slow.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.690
- I grew up in New Orleans.
- On top of COVID,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.490
having all of this.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:26.823
- Right, that's not we
- Anyway, I love,

00:02:26.823 --> 00:02:28.250
I really admire your work,

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.463
and I'm really,

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.174
I was really excited to
have this conversation,

00:02:32.174 --> 00:02:33.950
so thank you.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:34.910
- No, likewise.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:39.631
And clearly, the hurricane
is only one thing

00:02:39.631 --> 00:02:41.015
(laughing) that's going on in
everyone's lives right now,

00:02:41.015 --> 00:02:42.680
as you just mentioned COVID

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.880
and obviously something that
you've been very central

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.680
in is the conversation around how schools

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.500
should, could reopen and what
are the supports we need.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.130
So maybe a good place to start,

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.610
I just love to know where your head is.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.910
What are you doing on a day-to-day basis,

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.563
And how are you thinking about
the school opening situation?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.250
- So thank you for asking
the question that way.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.693
So, I mean my head,

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:18.410
is kind of bursting
all the time right now.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:22.910
Because this would be hard

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:23.920
regardless.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.830
If you had good leadership in the country,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.660
this would be hard.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.720
With leadership that is incompetent

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.270
and

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.183
still denying COVID exists,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.800
it makes it almost impossible
to try to figure out

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.530
how to get people the right information,

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.410
the science-based information

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.400
and how to keep communities safe.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.900
And so I find it very frustrating.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.020
I wanna scream most of
the time and I don't

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:01.500
because it's really important
to be heard right now.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.136
And it's important to make sure

00:04:03.136 --> 00:04:08.040
that people hear what
is accurate information,

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.910
even if they don't want to believe it.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.840
So we started

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.330
thinking about how to
reopen schools safely

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:21.090
in the beginning of April.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.880
Because we didn't wanna have

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.780
what happened in March happened again.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.775
The haphazard way that
schools were closed,

00:04:28.775 --> 00:04:30.110
our view was,

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:33.070
we were gonna learn as
much as we possibly could,

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:38.070
from as many of the
world-renowned epidemiologists,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.440
virologists, infectious
disease folks, as we could.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.900
And we had the advantage

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.480
that we are the second
largest nurse union,

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.780
not simply the second largest
largest teacher's union.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:53.420
So in April we put out a very,

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.520
we put out our first plan

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.220
about how do we open schools
and communities safely.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.280
And we spent a lot of
time talking to people

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.820
before we did that,
including our own members,

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.050
including parents

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.640
and including all the the
scientist I just talked about.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.540
We just put out another
one, an updated one

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.380
about a week or two ago.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.380
But frankly, even though we
know a lot more about the virus,

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:23.760
the safeguards are basically the same.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.930
You have to contain the virus

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.890
in a region.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.260
You have to maintain that containment

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:37.090
by testing, tracing and isolation.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:41.090
You have to have the school safeguards

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:45.280
that would prevent a virus
from spreading in the school,

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.490
which includes six feet
of physical distancing

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.210
and masks, cleaning and ventilation.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:54.110
And that's on top of
reasonably accommodating

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:57.812
those who are high risk and
obviously washing our hands.

00:05:57.812 --> 00:06:01.230
And you have to actually
have a way to pay for that.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.740
And that's just on the safety side.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:08.690
On the the wellbeing and
the instructional side,

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.650
we need to have a lot better way

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:15.530
of making sure remote
instruction can engage kids

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.760
in some ways like you
have done so successfully.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:23.260
And we also need to really
focus on wellbeing issues,

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:27.110
on digital divide issues and
on food and nutrition issues.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:30.310
So we've been trying to
do all of those things

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.643
at the same time in 3,500 locations.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:37.230
- No, it's not an enviable task.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.020
And I speak to a lot of
district superintendents

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.010
and administrators and teachers,

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.820
and everyone is in this really, really

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.450
difficult situation right now.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:46.990
I know, and we'll get into a little bit

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.660
of some of the contentious points about,

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.430
should a school be open or closed,

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.490
and distance learning,
good, bad, et cetera.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:57.490
But have you seen pockets
of people doing it well,

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.400
either at the district
level or at a state level?

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.450
- Yes, they're very, very quiet about it

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.420
because they don't want
people to follow them,

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:08.850
and they don't want, because
anyone who's doing it well,

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:12.130
knows that at any moment,
there could be a kid

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.960
or a teacher that tests
positive for COVID,

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.100
and then you have to
close down immediately

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.430
and you have to actually

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.850
go through all of the safety protocols

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:26.180
and then you pray that,

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.330
that people don't get sick.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.380
And or don't get very, very sick.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:34.593
So a lot of the places,
Like for example Newark,

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.230
had summer school.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:42.230
I frankly pushed for places
to do some summer schooling

00:07:42.721 --> 00:07:46.550
if they could, first and foremost,

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:50.020
because of the kids who really needed it,

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:54.680
who didn't connect well on

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:55.760
on the screens,

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.990
like you and I are having right now.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:01.730
But also to do it in a very safe way,

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.945
and in a way where we could learn things.

00:08:03.945 --> 00:08:08.810
And so in places like Detroit,
it didn't work very well.

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:12.450
But a place like Newark,
it worked pretty well.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.090
Or praise like BOCES in Suffolk County,

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.400
it worked pretty well.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.290
Montana, it worked pretty well.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.610
Now to me, what do I mean when
I say it worked pretty well?

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:25.390
It means one, there
were no negative cases,

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.570
there were no positive cases of COVID,

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:30.160
and kids came, teachers were there,

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.379
there were the safety measures in place.

00:08:32.379 --> 00:08:35.950
That is wonderful,

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.890
but it's also lucky.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.210
When I say Newark worked very well,

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:42.970
it's because there were a
couple of positive cases

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.670
and they handled it well.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.040
And they closed the school,

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.080
they communicated with
parents and with teachers,

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:52.890
they made sure that people
got tests immediately,

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.110
and they made sure they did
everything that they could

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.970
to keep kids and to keep
their, keep educators safe.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.613
And then before they reopened,

00:09:00.613 --> 00:09:02.720
they did all the kind of protocols,

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.680
including cleaning and everything

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:09.230
and contact tracing to make sure that,

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.290
that everybody who was in contact

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.363
with the person who tested positive,

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.700
they had gotten in contact with,

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.530
and those people were isolating.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:22.370
So that's the kind of
thing that you have to do.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.530
If you have like what has happened

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:28.210
in Gwinnett County in Georgia,

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.773
you see 240 people testing
positive in the first few days,

00:09:31.773 --> 00:09:33.590
that is a big problem.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.810
That is an SOS.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:37.160
That means you gotta have
a different structure.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.600
That's not close the school, close a pod,

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.530
see what happens.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.249
That means you've got
too much community spread

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:46.360
in that community, and you need
to be on remote instruction

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:49.430
because school should not
be open in that situation.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:52.790
So we're seeing

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.030
with both summer school,

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:58.790
as well as the starting
of the school year,

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.057
places that are doing it well

00:10:00.057 --> 00:10:02.320
and places that are doing it badly,

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.350
but we also don't have the
resources from Washington yet,

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.180
which we need very badly.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.530
And we also have a president who has been,

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:14.720
who is breeding chaos
instead of responsibility.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.110
This is the moment that you
need to be really responsible,

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:19.270
not chaotic.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:23.460
And his recklessness is
actually hurting things.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.560
I'll give you one example.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:29.510
In June, we polled our members.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:33.310
And remember, this was before
you saw this huge escalation

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.580
in the South and Southwest.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.727
And 75% of them said,

00:10:37.727 --> 00:10:40.440
that if we could get the safety safeguards

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.470
that we were advocating for,

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:45.630
they were comfortable with
going back to school buildings.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:50.510
Because they knew, how important
it was and it is for kids,

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:52.920
not just for feeding and
not just for wellbeing,

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.740
but for instruction as well.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.550
And so that, if I polled
my members right now,

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.423
you'd see the exact reverse.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.080
- And you see the reverse because
they don't have confidence

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.700
that some of the precautions

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.320
that you mentioned in the Newark place,

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.980
like the Newark context,

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:13.200
that those are in place,
that's where the fear is?

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:16.010
- I would say you'd see
it for four reasons.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:21.010
One, because of the
huge increase in spread

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.480
in the South and Southwest.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.640
Even though this week, you seem to have,

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.730
we have 14 states that are
hotspots rather than 18 States,

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.990
You still have 40 States,

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:36.600
where you see the line going like this,

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.990
as opposed to going like this.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:39.880
That is now

00:11:41.556 --> 00:11:43.320
and that's number one.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:46.870
Number two, you have a
president who is a denier.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.470
So yesterday he got on TV and said,

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.050
everything is going well,

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:53.500
even though Dr. Birx the day before,

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:58.500
said that things are really,
my words not her words.

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:00.030
Her words were

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:05.030
things were really
spreading very extensively.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.150
So number two is the
president's recklessness.

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:10.690
Number three, is that there's been

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:13.040
a lack of resources from Washington.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.870
So number four, the
planning that's been done,

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:20.530
is still in many, many
places, very, very vague,

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:25.530
because they planned hybrid,
but there's not a whole lot of,

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:29.070
meat behind,

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:31.520
there's not a lot of muscle
behind that planning.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.240
- If I'm understanding you correctly,

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:35.640
I mean, it makes a lot of sense.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:37.040
I'm just trying to think
through it logically.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.600
If you're in a part of the country

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:41.640
that has low community spread,

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.750
it can have some spread,
but low community spread,

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:45.780
but it seems like it's in control.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.570
Then open up in a very careful way,

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.990
have your contact tracing,
have the social distancing,

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:53.810
have the ventilation and keep track.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.660
And as soon as the contact tracing

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:58.640
traces contacts within a school,
you do have to shut down,

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.770
which makes all the sense in the world.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:01.603
- Right.
- And in places where

00:13:01.603 --> 00:13:03.656
you have high community spread,

00:13:03.656 --> 00:13:06.160
there's no point in trying to be physical

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.510
because you're very quickly
going to trigger a situation,

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:12.210
and you're gonna just
exacerbate the scenario.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.080
So that to me
- Yeah.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:16.690
- feels like a very reasonable,
I mean logical I don't,

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:19.370
somehow this is, it does feel
like it's gotten politicized.

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:20.680
When you look at the media,

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.990
it seems like there's
these kind of polar camps.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.350
One is kinda open schools no matter what,

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.620
and one is don't open
schools no matter what.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.540
And I'm definitely not
hearing that from you.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.880
- No, and it's different.

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:36.880
Look we have 50 States,
we have 98,000 schools,

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.880
we have 16,000 school districts.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:43.930
We've never had a one size
fits all for schooling

